From 7273ae1d1f54f2b1141fe09e92c82bd16902f064 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:17:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Gliding with a glider component added to the worn stack (the
 MekaSuit's Elytra Unit)

LivingEntity.canGlideUsing asks the stack: the minecraft:glider component may be the item's own or one added to the stack, so a mod's chestplate glides once its module puts the component on it. Items::glides checks both, with the wear rule, for the player and the server's guests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RYe92n7spgy8vtm4CovRWA
